  "summaries": [
    {
      "id": 113310,
      "category": "team",
      "content": "In this report, the researcher discovered that there was a cache poisoning weakness on `updates.rockstargames.com` due to an unkeyed header, `trailer`. By sending this header, an attacker could cause the cache to save a malformed response with status code 400. \n\nAn example of such a request, as provided by the researcher:\n\n```\nGET /patches/gtaiv/notes_title_update_6/GTAIVPC_TU6_Patch_Notes_FR.txt?donotpoisoneveryone=1 HTTP/1.1\nHost: updates.rockstargames.com\ntrailer: 1\n\n```\n\nTo resolve this issue, our team worked together with our CDN provider. The host no longer returns/saves a 400-code response when this header is sent in a request, and legitimate users can no longer be denied access to this content.",
      "updated_at": "2021-12-06T16:17:41.678Z",
      "can_view?": true,
      "can_create?": false,
